  {:id :state-belief-update :defines :s-next :node :R3
   :formal "For A(o|.) >= 0, B >= 0 with rows summing to 1, s_prev a distribution: pred(x) := sum_{s0} B(x|s0) s_prev(s0) (same index order as PolicyRollout.rolloutState); P(o) := sum_x A(o|x) pred(x); s_next(x) := A(o|x) pred(x) / P(o), or a typed refusal (none) exactly when P(o) = 0 (with A, B, s_prev >= 0: zero predictive probability). A returned s_next is a distribution. If P(o) > 0, for every distribution q: F_B.2(q; lik = A(o|.), prior = pred) = -ln P(o) iff q = s_next, and F_B.2(s_next) <= F_B.2(q): s_next is the unique minimiser of F. For s_prev a point mass at s0, s_next equals BeliefTrajectory.beliefUpdate (eq. 4.13 stationary belief, zero future term), refusal included, with no positivity hypotheses; for uncertain s_prev they differ (fixture: uniform prior, deterministic flip, noisy A, o = true: exact 9/10, mean-field refuses). Declared: one step, prior B s_prev (a filtering instance of B.2, not the trajectory F(pi)); no per-policy s_pi_tau, no future message, no smoothing, no gradient-flow dynamics"
   :spec-leg {:rung :formula-transcribed :licence "mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/ExactBeliefTrajectory.lean:52-70" :basis "exactUpdate (:56-61) states A(o|x) (B s_prev)(x) / P(o) with the typed none at P(o)=0; predictedState and observationProbability are the same index order PolicyRollout uses (verified by reading the file at HEAD)."}
   :impl-leg {:rung :formula-transcribed :licence "src/futon2/aif/cascade_model_manifest.clj:944-992" :basis "exact-update (:944) and token-belief-at (:972) transcribe the Lean statement in exact rationals, typed zero-predictive-probability refusal included; the docstrings name ExactBeliefTrajectory.exactUpdate. Live-caller status is the open WM-02 question (reached at horizon-g/token-belief seams; not shown wired into the tick's stored belief); no run identity, so :witnessed is not licensed."}
   :leading-leg :level :certificate {:trailing-leg :both :reason "Both legs state the formula; no accepted-run certificate ties a run-identified stored-belief trajectory to independent per-step posteriors." :what-would-license "A run-identified multi-step belief trajectory with independent A/B/q reconstruction per step and a refusing verdict, in the branch the tick actually stores."} :converged? false}

