  {:id :adjudication-rates :defines :rates :node :R7
   :formal "Per truth kind: false-neg := P(recorded verdict = false | admitted = :present), false-pos := P(recorded verdict = true | admitted = :absent), as RAW exact-rational counts, numerator over denominator. An error count exists only where BOTH a recorded verdict and an admitted reference are present for the same subject. A zero denominator is :unobserved for that cell -- never 0, never defaulted. No default prior, no smoothing; a prior applies only when passed explicitly with an :authority, and an unauthorised prior refuses. THE READER (A-S Revision 3): a token class enters only when BOTH cells have a denominator of at least 5; the estimate is A-S section 2's Jeffreys Beta(1/2, 1/2) passed as an authorised prior; a class below the minimum or with one cell unobserved is left out of the labels (so it reaches the kernel wholly unobserved: the zero kernel as the unmeasured default for a checkable class) and recorded as excluded with its counts, never refusing the whole call; one label per subject and check-code sha."
   :spec-leg {:rung :formula-transcribed, :licence "mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Proof2/AdjudicationCounts.lean:331-348", :basis "adjudicationRatesOf builds the kernel's rate table from counted cells, each rate numerator over denominator (rateAt over cellOf), and is only applied under FullyMeasured, so no cell's :unobserved is ever read as 0. Committed at mathlib4 87aaf5edda (C2), read at 8f5e11fe78 (CONV-I, claude-14). The optional prior-with-:authority branch is not modelled: the Lean is the raw-count case the formal makes the default."}
   :impl-leg {:rung :formula-transcribed, :licence "src/futon2/aif/observation_rates.clj:32-107", :basis "cell (:32-45) counts compared labels (recorded verdict present), numerator over denominator as exact rationals, and returns {:status :unobserved} on a zero denominator; rates-by-class (:75-107) fills both truth kinds per class; the prior is nil or {:alpha :beta :authority} and refuses otherwise (:63-66). Read at futon2 c4f20ec8."}
   :leading-leg :level :certificate {:trailing-leg :both, :reason "not found: No run-identified record carries measured rates checked against an independent recount.", :what-would-license "A run-identified adjudication record whose per-class rates are recomputed from its labels and match."} :converged? false}

  {:id :co-application-kernel :defines :B-co :node :R4
   :formal "K(s, .) := every unit on the ENABLED FRONTIER of r at s fires independently with its own theta; each subset S of the frontier that succeeds, with probability prod_S theta * prod_(F\\S) (1 - theta), moves s to s union produces(S). An empty frontier is {s -> 1}. The frontier at s is the enabled units with no enabled unit strictly above them in r. K = cascadeKernel (the one-at-a-time list kernel) exactly on a chain. A theta outside [0,1] refuses."
