   :formal "r := the containment order over UNITS -- one node per APPLICATION of a pattern, the pattern id as an attribute, so a cascade applying one pattern twice has two units. Unit A is above unit B iff A produces a token B's guard needs. Below is reflexive (a = b or Reach r a b); the semilattice condition is restricted to OVERLAPPING pairs (those sharing a descendant), and an overlapping pair without a meet is the typed finding :missing-meets naming the pair and the maximal units of its common part, not a failure. A cyclic containment REFUSES with :cyclic-containment. A precedence list is the chain case of r."
