  {:id :target-grain-g :defines :Delta-G-t :node :R5
   :formal "Under a POSITIVE PRODUCT-form preference C(o) = prod_v (c_in v if v in o else c_out v), total G = risk + ambiguity is minus a sum of per-token terms. Partition the tokens into t's own U and the rest: if the candidate law q1 and the baseline q2 have the same total mass and the same present-marginal on every token OUTSIDE U, then G(q1) - G(q2) = localDelta U q1 q2, the delta over U alone. Two targets are then comparable by their localised deltas. When the action also moves a token outside U, localDelta misreports by EXACTLY the outside tokens' term difference."
   :spec-leg {:rung :formula-transcribed, :licence "mathlib4/DarkTower/WarMachine/Proof2/TargetGrainG.lean:56-92", :basis "localDelta (:60-61) and deltaG_localises (:87-92): under a positive product preference, equal mass and equal present-marginals outside U, G(q1) - G(q2) = localDelta U q1 q2. Committed at mathlib4 759b8ca884, read at 8f5e11fe78."}
   :impl-leg {:rung :named, :licence "src/futon2/aif/target_field.clj:278-308", :basis "with-pair-overlap implements only the theorem's comparability hypothesis (a constructed candidate moves no token of the other target's universe) and types the absences; nothing computes localDelta or a target-grain Delta-G, and no target has a constructed candidate at HEAD. Read at futon2 c4f20ec8."}
   :leading-leg :spec-ahead :certificate {:trailing-leg :impl, :reason "not found: The runtime records comparability only; no target-grain Delta-G is computed.", :what-would-license "A runtime localDelta over a target's universe, then a run-identified comparison of two targets' deltas."} :converged? false}

